SUMMARY:Deadline: Spencer Education Journalism Fellowship 2027-28 (Columbia
  Journalism School)
DESCRIPTION:The Spencer Education Journalism Fellowship\, based at Columbia
  Journalism School\, supports ambitious\, research-savvy storytellers prod
 ucing books\, magazine features\, documentaries and podcasts that deepen p
 ublic understanding of critical issues in education. Reporters with educat
 ion or related-field experience\, and educators with journalism experience
 \, are especially encouraged.\n\nOrganisation: Spencer Fellowship at Colum
 bia Journalism School\nLocation: New York City\, USA (residential) or anyw
 here in the US (non-residential\, with several paid trips to NYC). Open to
  US citizens and permanent residents only.\nAward: Residential stipend USD
  85\,000 or non-residential stipend USD 43\,000\, plus a USD 7\,500 travel
  and research budget. Non-residential fellows also get airfare and hotel f
 or required NYC trips. No application fee.\nDuration: One academic year (2
 027-28).\n\nMore: https://spencerfellows.org/how-to-apply-2/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://spencerfellows.org/how-to-apply-2/?utm_source=artificialnouveau
 grantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York City\, USA (residential) or anywhere in the US (non-resid
 ential\, with several paid trips to NYC). Open to US citizens and permanen
 t residents only.
END:VEVENT
