SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 EST: New America Fellows Program\, Class of 2028 (US
 D 15\,000 to 30\,000 unrestricted for nonfiction books\, films\, podcasts 
 and multimedia in progress)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Feb 2027 at 23:59 EST.\n\nNew America\, the Washingto
 n think tank\, runs a one-year fellowship for writers\, journalists\, film
 makers and other storytellers finishing an ambitious nonfiction reporting 
 project.\n\nOrganisation: New America\nLocation: Nonresidential: Fellows s
 tay in their jobs and home city. Two required in-person gatherings in Wash
 ington\, DC\, USA (opening\, week of 4 October 2027\; closing\, May 2028)\
 , with travel\, lodging and most meals covered\, plus monthly virtual gath
 erings. Non-US citizens and applicants based abroad may apply.\nAward: Unr
 estricted stipend of USD 15\,000 to 30\,000\, typically paid in three inst
 alments directly to the Fellow (not to an institution). The level varies b
 y class and by the funding secured that year. Travel\, lodging and most me
 als for the two Washington gatherings are covered. Team projects receive t
 he same amount as an individual. No application fee stated.\nDuration: 9 m
 onths (September 2027 to May 2028)\n\nMore: https://www.newamerica.org/fel
 lowships/new-america-fellows/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://www.newamerica.org/fellowships/new-america-fellows/?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Nonresidential: Fellows stay in their jobs and home city. Two requ
 ired in-person gatherings in Washington\, DC\, USA (opening\, week of 4 Oc
 tober 2027\; closing\, May 2028)\, with travel\, lodging and most meals co
 vered\, plus monthly virtual gatherings. Non-US citizens and applicants ba
 sed abroad may apply.
